CLAUDE CODE
Reviewed all source: audioinfo.go, config.go, server.go, types.go,
cmd/audioinfo/main.go, audioinfo_api.ts, audioinfo_player.ts, tests, Makefile.
Four issues found:

1. buildBrowseQuery / parseQuery MISMATCH (bug): buildBrowseQuery produces
   album:"multi word" but parseQuery tokenises on whitespace, splitting quoted
   phrases into broken tokens. Multi-word album/artist/title browse silently fails.

2. GetArtists NOT SORTED: deduplication uses a Go map, giving non-deterministic
   order. GetAlbums and GetTitles both use ORDER BY; GetArtists does not.

3. NO BUNDLE TARGET: audioinfo_player.ts and audioinfo_api.ts exist but there
   is no Makefile target to produce htdocs/module/audioinfo.js, and htdocs/
   does not exist. The web UI cannot be used end-to-end.

4. DURATION NEVER POPULATED: ProcessAudioFile reads tags but github.com/dhowden/tag
   does not expose audio duration. Duration field is always empty after a scan.
   Browser player recovers via loadedmetadata; CLI show and API /api/show/{id}
   always display empty.

Questions before proceeding:
Q1: For the multi-word fix, add quoted-phrase parsing to Go parseQuery, or switch
    TypeScript buildBrowseQuery to /regex/ form?
Q2: Should htdocs/ live inside the audioinfo/ repo, or be user-configured only?
Q3: Duration via ffprobe, or accept browser-only for now?


